"living in the margins" home + studio / 2025\
\'93living in the margins\'94
\f1\b0  reframes marginal space as a productive condition for living and making. The project addresses the challenge of integrating private residential life, public creative programs, and an existing structure without dividing the building into conventional enclosed rooms.\
Six continuous two-foot-thick walls establish the building\'92s horizontal order while minimizing vertical partitions. A ten-foot band between the two primary walls concentrates the bedroom, private studio, and circulation, using changes in floor elevation to create privacy and intimacy within a constrained width. Public programs\'97including the gallery and living spaces\'97expand outward into larger, more open volumes.\
The margin also resolves the junction between old and new. A recessed, frosted steel-framed gap maintains visual separation while accommodating differential movement, while an offset GFRC screen and thin roof reinforce the project\'92s horizontal expression. Together, these strategies transform edges, gaps, and residual zones into active spaces for occupation, mediation, and transition.\
